        "original_id": "bc3a86a8-25cd-558f-9343-a598f1e96273",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Dear America series\n- Events: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: American history topics\n\nFacts:\n- The Dear America series covers many American history topics, including the Pilgrims' journey, the Salem Witch Trials, the French and Indian War, the American Revolution, the American Civil War, World War I, World War II, western expansion, slavery, immigration, prairie life, the California Gold Rush, the Great Depression, Native Americans' experiences, racism, coal mining, the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire, women's suffrage, the sinking of the RMS Titanic, the Battle of the Alamo, and the Vietnam War.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire occurred in New York City on March 25, 1911.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire was the deadliest industrial disaster in New York City history and one of the deadliest industrial disasters in United States history.",
